      "source_number": "181",
      "independent_solution": "The actual table gives Mercury 3.17*10^23 kg, Venus 4.87*10^24 kg, Earth 5.98*10^24 kg, Mars 6.40*10^23 kg, Jupiter 1.90*10^27 kg, Saturn 5.69*10^26 kg, Uranus 8.70*10^25 kg, Neptune 1.03*10^26 kg, Pluto 5.40*10^24 kg. Normalize or compare powers of ten first, then coefficients within the same order: Mercury < Mars < Venus < Pluto < Earth < Uranus < Neptune < Saturn < Jupiter. In particular Neptune is heavier than Uranus despite 1.03 < 8.70, and Pluto lies between Venus and Earth. Jupiter/Earth = (1.90/5.98)*10^3 = 95000/299 = 317.7257525..., approximately 318 times; this ratio is dimensionless.",
      "tasks": [
        "Order all nine listed bodies by increasing mass, using both exponents and coefficients.",
        "Compute the directed Jupiter-to-Earth mass ratio, including the 10^3 exponent factor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_number": "183",
      "independent_solution": "For x != 0, intersections of y=6/x with y=x-1 solve 6=x^2-x, hence (x-3)(x+2)=0 and x=-2 or 3. The intersection coordinates are (-2,-3) and (3,2). Intersections of y=6/x with y=x+3 solve 6=x^2+3x, hence x=(-3-sqrt(33))/2 or (-3+sqrt(33))/2, approximately -4.3722813 or 1.3722813. Their y coordinates are approximately -1.3722813 and 4.3722813 respectively. The hyperbola has one branch in quadrant I and one in quadrant III, excludes x=0, and approaches both axes. The two source lines have slope 1 and y intercepts -1 and +3; the second is four units above the first. Algebra independently checks the graphical readings; it does not replace the source's graph-method learning task. Source 183 declares no source figure.",
      "tasks": [
        "Construct or interpret the graph pair y=6/x and y=x-1 and read both intersection abscissae.",
        "Construct or interpret the graph pair y=6/x and y=x+3 and read both intersection abscissae."
      ]
    }
  ],
